{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "The approval primitive's request digest and challenge binding (docs/page-actions.md §6). request_sha256 is bare lowercase hex of SHA-256 over aweb.approval-request/1\\n followed by the canonical JSON of {policy: {ref, version}, request}. The challenge binding is the raw 32-byte SHA-256 over aweb.approval-challenge/1\\n followed by the canonical JSON of its fields, shown here as hex. The fields are approval_id, candidate_subject and candidate_subject_type (the candidate the proof is for), nonce (hex), policy_ref, policy_version, purpose, request_sha256 and task_answer_ref, which is always present, null when there is no task answer. `requester_cases` pin the requester rule at mint and at decide (docs/page-actions.md §6): principals are named by role in the case, each decide step starts from the minted approval, and both sides are compared as aweb_naapp.roles.principal_key values. Refusals apply to the whole covered object.",
